# The rescue system of the uc-pxx boot initramfs (busybox init). /init starts
# it when the root file system cannot start. It runs from RAM.
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
# The LCD shows the rescue screen (tsx-rescue-status of tsx-linux-common).
# Enter on a USB keyboard (tty1) opens a root shell on the LCD.
tty1::respawn:/usr/sbin/tsx-rescue-status loop
# A root shell on the serial console (ttyS2, 115200, the debug UART). Only a
# person with the debug cable can reach it.
::respawn:/bin/sh -c "[ -c /dev/ttyS2 ] && exec /sbin/getty -n -l /bin/sh -L 115200 ttyS2 vt100 || exec sleep 2147483647"
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
# The last shutdown step: uc-pxx-reboot loader|fastboot leaves the mode in
# /run/uc-pxx-reboot.mode, and this line restarts with it after the system
# is stopped. Without the file it does nothing.
::shutdown:/usr/sbin/uc-pxx-reboot --pending
